---
/**
 * LATEST NEWS & EVENTS — audit §11.
 *
 * ═══ SIX SECTIONS, ONE PAGE ════════════════════════════════════════════════
 *
 * The audit names six things that must "always remain current": recent
 * achievements, school events, competitions, workshops, celebrations and
 * important announcements. They are six SECTIONS of one page, and the client
 * settled it by removing the dropdown that used to make Notices a separate
 * destination.
 *
 * A page that must stay current can only stay current if it is SHORT. So this
 * is the recency layer — a rail per category, a handful of items each — and
 * every category ends in a button to the archive that actually holds the
 * volume:
 *
 *   Achievements   → /beyond-academics/achievements/
 *   School events  → /news-events/school-events/
 *   Competitions   → /news-events/competitions/
 *   Workshops      → /news-events/workshops/
 *   Celebrations   → /news-events/celebrations/
 *   Announcements  → /news-events/notices/
 *
 * Four of those six are now full sub-pages of their own (data/newsPages.ts),
 * built once the school's site was read properly and turned out to hold fourteen
 * named workshops and thirty-five dated events. Achievements keeps its existing
 * home; announcements has no source content yet — the school's /notice/ pages
 * are empty — so it stays a section here until assets A7 and C7 land.
 *
 * That split is the whole design. The live School Activities page carries 148
 * headings and 4,536 images on a single URL — measured — which is what happens
 * when the recency layer and the archive are the same page.
 *
 * ⚠ THIS FILE RETIRES A PLACEHOLDER AUTOMATICALLY. `/news-events/` was one of
 * the generated not-yet-built pages; a real file at this path takes precedence
 * and drops out of that generator's list with no other edit. Deleting this file
 * restores the placeholder rather than producing a 404 — which is the point of
 * building it that way.
 *
 * ⚠ NOT ONE ITEM IS INVENTED, and there are no dates anywhere. See the header of
 * data/newsEvents.ts: every card is content the school has already published,
 * and a static build cannot honestly print "latest" against a date it baked in
 * months earlier. Dates arrive with asset A7 — which also brings the named
 * publishing owner audit §11 depends on (C7). Without that this page is stale by
 * March, and no amount of design prevents it.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import CardGrid from '../../components/news/CardGrid.astro';

import { getChroniclePage } from '../../lib/cms';;
import heroPhoto from '../../assets/photos/sunbeem-4.jpg';

const achievementsPage = await getChroniclePage('achievements');

/* No two adjacent categories share a ground — the page's only structural rule,
   and with six near-identical sections it is doing real work. */
---

<BaseLayout
>
  <PageHero
    src={heroPhoto}
  />

  {/* ⚠ THE SECTION RAIL IS GONE WITH THE OTHER STREAMS. It was a jump list
      across six categories; with one section left it would be a navigation
      control pointing at a single destination — the same "control that does
      nothing" the pager guards against elsewhere. */}

  {/* padding-block: 0 — every section carries its own --sb-section-y, and the
      panel adding its own on top is what put a 183px void under the hero on
      three earlier pages. */}
  <div class="u-page-panel news-panel">
    <CardGrid page={achievementsPage} base="/news-events/achievements/" unit="achievement" />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.news-panel { padding-block: 0; }

  .news-panel :global(section[id]) {
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--sb-masthead-h) + 24px);
  }
</style>
